---
// Why sort order helps a column store compress, as a left/right showdown:
// the same eight sale_date values in arrival order and sorted, and the sorted
// column collapsed into runs (value, count). The KB figures at the bottom are
// measured on the 10-million-row Parquet files from the DuckDB run in the post.
// Plain inline SVG with site tokens; no ids.

const W = 900;
const H = 440;

const unsorted = ['2024-03-02', '2024-03-01', '2024-03-03', '2024-03-02', '2024-03-01', '2024-03-02', '2024-03-01', '2024-03-02'];
const sorted = [...unsorted].sort();
const runs: { value: string; start: number; count: number }[] = [];
sorted.forEach((v, i) => {
  const last = runs[runs.length - 1];
  if (last && last.value === v) last.count++;
  else runs.push({ value: v, start: i, count: 1 });
});

const cellW = 150;
const cellH = 26;
const cellGap = 4;
const top = 104;
const leftX = 20;
const rightX = 470;
const runX = rightX + cellW + 64;
const runW = 166;
const cellY = (i: number) => top + i * (cellH + cellGap);
---
<figure class="srt">
  <div class="srt-scroll">
  <svg viewBox={`0 0 ${W} ${H}`} role="img" aria-label="Eight sale_date values. In arrival order, neighbouring values differ. Sorted, equal dates sit together and the column can be stored as three runs: 2024-03-01 three times, 2024-03-02 four times, 2024-03-03 once. In the measured 10-million-row Parquet file the sale_date column took 11,368 KB unsorted and 8 KB sorted.">
    <text x={leftX} y="24" class="srt-h">
      <tspan data-lang-en>Stored in arrival order</tspan>
      <tspan data-lang-vi>Lưu theo thứ tự đến</tspan>
    </text>
    <text x={leftX} y="46" class="srt-sub">
      <tspan data-lang-en>Neighbouring values differ, so there is little to squeeze.</tspan>
      <tspan data-lang-vi>Giá trị cạnh nhau khác nhau, nên khó nén.</tspan>
    </text>
    <text x={rightX} y="24" class="srt-h">
      <tspan data-lang-en>Sorted by sale_date, then product_id</tspan>
      <tspan data-lang-vi>Sắp theo sale_date, rồi tới product_id</tspan>
    </text>
    <text x={rightX} y="46" class="srt-sub">
      <tspan data-lang-en>Equal values sit together, so each run is stored once.</tspan>
      <tspan data-lang-vi>Giá trị giống nhau nằm liền nhau, mỗi đoạn lưu một lần.</tspan>
    </text>
    <line x1="20" x2={W - 20} y1="64" y2="64" class="srt-rule" />

    <text x={leftX} y={top - 12} class="srt-field">sale_date</text>
    {unsorted.map((v, i) => (
      <g>
        <rect x={leftX} y={cellY(i)} width={cellW} height={cellH} rx="3" class="srt-cell" />
        <text x={leftX + cellW / 2} y={cellY(i) + 18} text-anchor="middle" class="srt-in">{v}</text>
      </g>
    ))}

    <text x={rightX} y={top - 12} class="srt-field">sale_date</text>
    {sorted.map((v, i) => (
      <g>
        <rect x={rightX} y={cellY(i)} width={cellW} height={cellH} rx="3" class="srt-cell" />
        <text x={rightX + cellW / 2} y={cellY(i) + 18} text-anchor="middle" class="srt-in">{v}</text>
      </g>
    ))}

    <text x={runX} y={top - 12} class="srt-field">
      <tspan data-lang-en>stored as runs</tspan>
      <tspan data-lang-vi>lưu thành từng đoạn (run)</tspan>
    </text>
    {runs.map((r) => {
      const y1 = cellY(r.start);
      const y2 = cellY(r.start + r.count - 1) + cellH;
      const mid = (y1 + y2) / 2;
      const bx = rightX + cellW + 10;
      return (
        <g>
          <path d={`M${bx},${y1 + 3} L${bx + 8},${y1 + 3} L${bx + 8},${y2 - 3} L${bx},${y2 - 3}`} class="srt-brace" />
          <path d={`M${bx + 8},${mid} L${runX - 8},${mid}`} class="srt-brace" />
          <polygon points={`${runX - 9},${mid - 5} ${runX - 9},${mid + 5} ${runX - 1},${mid}`} class="srt-head" />
          <rect x={runX} y={mid - cellH / 2} width={runW} height={cellH} rx="3" class="srt-cell is-run" />
          <text x={runX + runW / 2} y={mid + 5} text-anchor="middle" class="srt-in is-run">
            <tspan data-lang-en>{`${r.value} × ${r.count}`}</tspan>
            <tspan data-lang-vi>{`${r.value} × ${r.count}`}</tspan>
          </text>
        </g>
      );
    })}

    <line x1="20" x2={W - 20} y1="364" y2="364" class="srt-rule" />
    <text x={leftX} y="392" class="srt-label">
      <tspan data-lang-en>Measured, 10M rows: sale_date column</tspan>
      <tspan data-lang-vi>Đo thật, 10 triệu dòng: cột sale_date</tspan>
    </text>
    <text x={leftX} y="424" class="srt-num is-bad">
      <tspan data-lang-en>11,368 KB</tspan>
      <tspan data-lang-vi>11.368 KB</tspan>
    </text>
    <text x={rightX} y="392" class="srt-label">
      <tspan data-lang-en>Measured, 10M rows: sale_date column</tspan>
      <tspan data-lang-vi>Đo thật, 10 triệu dòng: cột sale_date</tspan>
    </text>
    <text x={rightX} y="424" class="srt-num">8 KB</text>
  </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption>
    <span data-lang-en>Eight values are enough to show the idea; the numbers at the bottom are the sale_date column inside the two Parquet files from the DuckDB run above (366 distinct dates, zstd compression). Sorting has to move whole rows, so only the first sort key gets runs this long.</span>
    <span data-lang-vi>Tám giá trị là đủ thấy ý tưởng; con số bên dưới là cột sale_date trong hai file Parquet ở lần chạy DuckDB phía trên (366 ngày khác nhau, nén zstd). Sắp xếp phải dời nguyên cả dòng, nên chỉ cột sắp xếp đầu tiên mới có các đoạn dài như vậy.</span>
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .srt {
    margin: 2em 0;
    width: 100%;
  }
  .srt-scroll {
    overflow-x: auto;
  }
  .srt svg {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    min-width: 640px;
    height: auto;
  }
  .srt text {
    font-size: 14px;
    fill: var(--text-body);
  }
  .srt .srt-h {
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: 700;
    fill: var(--text);
  }
  .srt .srt-sub,
  .srt .srt-label {
    fill: var(--text-muted);
  }
  .srt .srt-field {
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 600;
    fill: var(--text-muted);
  }
  .srt-rule {
    stroke: var(--border);
  }
  .srt-cell {
    fill: var(--bg-alt);
    stroke: var(--border);
    stroke-width: 1.2;
  }
  .srt-cell.is-run {
    fill: var(--red-tint-bg);
    stroke: var(--red);
    stroke-width: 1.6;
  }
  .srt .srt-in {
    font-size: 13px;
    fill: var(--text);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  .srt .srt-in.is-run {
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .srt-brace {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--text-muted);
    stroke-width: 1.3;
  }
  .srt-head {
    fill: var(--text-muted);
  }
  .srt .srt-num {
    font-size: 28px;
    font-weight: 700;
    fill: var(--text);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  .srt .srt-num.is-bad {
    fill: var(--red);
  }
  .srt figcaption {
    margin-top: 10px;
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.55;
    text-align: center;
  }
</style>
